  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let \\(a<b<c\\) be three real numbers and \\(\\omega\\) denote a complex cube root of unity. If \\((a+b\\omega+c\\omega^2)^3+(a+b\\omega^2+c\\omega)^3=0\\), then which of the following must be true?",
  "options": {
    "A": "\\(a+b+c=0\\)",
    "B": "\\(abc=0\\)",
    "C": "\\(ab+bc+ca=0\\)",
    "D": "\\(b=\\frac{c+a}{2}\\)"
  },
  "answer": "D",
